# Dockerfile-specific override of the root .dockerignore, used by BuildKit for
# this Dockerfile ONLY (ops/Dockerfile and scripts/release-build.sh keep using
# the unmodified root .dockerignore).
#
# Why this file exists: the root .dockerignore has a blanket `*.sh` rule
# (line 83) written for ops/Dockerfile's source-compilation path. This
# Dockerfile instead COPYs a real, checked-in docker-entrypoint.sh into the
# runtime stage, so that one script IS needed for this build. The root file
# must not be modified — ops/Dockerfile and scripts/release-build.sh depend
# on it as-is.
#
# Why `*` is safe here (unlike duplicating the root ruleset): this Dockerfile
# COPYs exactly one file from the host build context — docker-entrypoint.sh.
# Everything else it needs comes from COPY --from=fetch (a separate build
# stage) or curl (fetched from GitHub releases at build time). Ignoring
# everything except that one file is equivalent to the root ruleset for this
# Dockerfile's purposes, without hand-duplicating 129 lines that would then
# silently drift out of sync with future edits to the root file.
*
!docker-entrypoint.sh
